  "details": "Version:  2019.2.4 (possibly earlier versions too)\n\n(EDIT: I've now found it seems to happen regardless of whether there is a vrc station or not)\n\nI'm making a simple \"ride\".   Two boats take two players around the world.  Both boats have an animator, a vrc_station,  and object sync. For my test, the animation lasts around 15 seconds.  When testing the world by myself it works great.  When I try it with a friend though,  from my perspective the ride suddenly restarts halfway through,  but to the other person it looks normal (I make it to the end of the ride).  \n\nI've tried both with and without an exit time on the animation. Looping is turned off.  So it seems like a syncing issue to me.\n\nRepro steps:\nMake two objects and add a vrc_station and vrc_objectsync to both.  \nCreate a simple animation for both to move the object forward for 15-20secs or more, and an animator.\nMake a button to start/stop the animation.\nTest with two people or more. \n\nExample test world:\nwrld_8a783b82-8bc9-47ad-9586-ab5697faa2fa",
